@page "/components/datagrid/filtering"

<DocsPage>
    <DocsPageHeader Title="DataGrid - Filtering" Component="@nameof(VekDataGrid<T>)">
        <Description>
            Learn about DataGrid filtering modes, column filter menus, row filtering, case-sensitivity, and customized filter templates.
        </Description>
    </DocsPageHeader>
    <DocsPageContent>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Filtering Overview">
                <Description>
                    <CodeInline>&lt;VekDataGrid></CodeInline> supports filtering with several <CodeInline>DataGridFilterMode</CodeInline> settings through the <CodeInline>FilterMode</CodeInline> parameter.
                    <br>
                    • <CodeInline>Simple</CodeInline> is the <b>default</b>. All filters are managed in a single popover, and you can set multiple filters across multiple columns.
                    <br>
                    • <CodeInline>ColumnFilterMenu</CodeInline> provides a dedicated popover for each column.
                    <br>
                    • <CodeInline>ColumnFilterRow</CodeInline> places the filtering UI inline in the grid.
                    <br><br>
                    String filtering case sensitivity can be configured globally with <CodeInline>FilterCaseSensitivity</CodeInline>.
                    <br><br>
                    For backend data scenarios, see <VekLink Href="/components/datagrid/virtualization#server-side-filtering-sorting-and-pagination">Server Side Filtering, Sorting and Pagination</VekLink>.
                    <br /><br/>
                    QuickFilter is shown in the <VekLink Href="/components/datagrid#advanced-data-grid">Advanced Data Grid</VekLink> example.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>

            <DocsPageSection>
                <SectionHeader Title="Basic">
                    <Description>
                        This example demonstrates the built-in filtering UI using the same items and paging setup. Use it to compare each <CodeInline>DataGridFilterMode</CodeInline> option and see how <CodeInline>FilterCaseSensitivity</CodeInline> affects string filtering.
                    </Description>
                </SectionHeader>
                <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridFilteringExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                    <DataGridFilteringExample />
                </SectionContent>
            </DocsPageSection>

            <DocsPageSection>
                <SectionHeader Title="Simple FilterTemplate">
                    <Description>
                        In <CodeInline>DataGridFilterMode.Simple</CodeInline>, you can keep the built-in simple filter panel and customize a column with <CodeInline>&lt;Column&gt;.&lt;FilterTemplate&gt;</CodeInline>, or replace the panel with <CodeInline>&lt;VekDataGrid&gt;.&lt;FilterTemplate&gt;</CodeInline>. This example uses a toggle to switch between those two approaches.
                        <br /><br />
                        <CodeInline>&lt;VekDataGrid&gt;.&lt;FilterTemplate&gt;</CodeInline> receives <CodeInline>VekDataGrid&lt;T&gt;</CodeInline>, while <CodeInline>&lt;Column&gt;.&lt;FilterTemplate&gt;</CodeInline> receives <CodeInline>FilterContext&lt;T&gt;</CodeInline>. <CodeInline>FilterContext&lt;T&gt;</CodeInline> provides the active filter definition and actions to apply, clear, or close the current filter UI. These actions operate on the filter UI surface that owns the template.
                        <br /><br />
                        The Category column template maps selected values to the active filter definition and applies a custom <CodeInline>FilterFunction</CodeInline> for multi-select matching. The grid template replaces the built-in panel and syncs the custom Name and Category inputs to the grid filters. For exact member details, see the API section.
                    </Description>
                </SectionHeader>
                <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridFilterTemplateSimpleModeExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                    <DataGridFilterTemplateSimpleModeExample />
                </SectionContent>
            </DocsPageSection>

            <DocsPageSection>
                <SectionHeader Title="Row and Menu FilterTemplate">
                    <Description>
                        <CodeInline>&lt;Column&gt;.&lt;FilterTemplate&gt;</CodeInline> also works in <CodeInline>DataGridFilterMode.ColumnFilterRow</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>DataGridFilterMode.ColumnFilterMenu</CodeInline>. These modes also use <CodeInline>FilterContext&lt;T&gt;</CodeInline>, so the same context shape is reused while <CodeInline>Actions</CodeInline> operate on the currently rendered filter UI.
                        <br /><br />
                        This example keeps the built-in filter behavior for most columns and overrides one column with a custom multi-select filter. In <CodeInline>DataGridFilterMode.ColumnFilterMenu</CodeInline>, the filter is applied manually through the grid so the menu can stay open while selections change. For exact member details, see the <VekLink Href="/api/vekdatagrid">API</VekLink> section.
                    </Description>
                </SectionHeader>
                <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridAdvancedFilteringExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                    <DataGridAdvancedFilteringExample />
                </SectionContent>
            </DocsPageSection>

            <DocsPageSection>
                <SectionHeader Title="Search Panel & Highlighting">
                    <Description>
                        Enable a built-in search box with <CodeInline>ShowSearchBox="true"</CodeInline>. By default, search terms evaluate across all searchable columns using <CodeInline>DataGridSearchTextParseMode.GroupWordsByAnd</CodeInline> (all words must match). You can switch to <CodeInline>GroupWordsByOr</CodeInline> or <CodeInline>ExactMatch</CodeInline> via <CodeInline>SearchTextParseMode</CodeInline>.
                        <br><br>
                        Columns can be excluded from search with <CodeInline>AllowSearch="false"</CodeInline>. Matching substrings inside data cells are automatically highlighted with <CodeInline>&lt;mark&gt;</CodeInline> tags when <CodeInline>HighlightSearchResults="true"</CodeInline> (default).
                    </Description>
                </SectionHeader>
                <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridSearchPanelExample)" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                    <DataGridSearchPanelExample />
                </SectionContent>
            </DocsPageSection>

            <DocsPageSection>
                <SectionHeader Title="Advanced Filter Row">
                    <Description>
                        Enable a dedicated inline filter row beneath column headers by setting <CodeInline>ShowFilterRow="true"</CodeInline>.
                        Each column provides comparison operator selectors (such as <CodeInline>Equals</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>Contains</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>StartsWith</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>Between</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>GreaterThan</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>LessThan</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>IsNull</CodeInline>, and <CodeInline>IsNotNull</CodeInline>) with debounced input configured via <CodeInline>FilterRowInputDelay</CodeInline> (default 300ms).
                        <br /><br />
                        Individual columns can configure their default operator using <CodeInline>FilterOperator</CodeInline> and enable or disable filtering using <CodeInline>AllowFiltering</CodeInline>.
                    </Description>
                </SectionHeader>
                <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridAdvancedFilterRowExample)" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                    <DataGridAdvancedFilterRowExample />
                </SectionContent>
            </DocsPageSection>

        </DocsPageSection>

    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>